WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/settings/components/ResetSection.tsx — a settings feature component (named export) rendered
  under <section id="reset"> on the Settings page. It is mutation-only (no remote read / query) and composes:
    • useResetSection(section) → POST /settings/reset { section }  (one mutation per whitelisted section)
    • useResetAllSettings()    → POST /settings/reset {}            (the Danger-zone global reset)
    • SudoCanceledError (from the shared request() client's transparent step-up replay) — swallowed as a non-error
    • useToast().success + useMutationToast().error                 (post-action feedback)  · useTranslation (t)
    • useSectionRows() / useDeniedRows()                            (two constant useMemo catalogs)
  Structure: three stacked GlassPanels — (1) "Reset to defaults": header (IconBox amber RotateCcw + title +
  subtitle) + a divide-y list of the 8 whitelisted sections (IconBox cyan + title + description + a per-row ghost
  "Reset" button, busy only for the section being reset); (2) read-only deny-list: header (IconBox cyan Shield +
  title + subtitle) + 2 rows (tariffs, sound_prefs) each AlertTriangle + title + reason; (3) Danger zone (red
  border): header (IconBox red AlertOctagon) + a HelperText + a danger "Reset ALL settings" button. Plus two
  ConfirmDialogs: a per-section danger dialog (title "Reset {name}?", message "{description} This action is
  permanent.") and the global danger dialog with requireTypedConfirmation="RESET" (confirm disabled until the
  user types RESET). On success a toast announces "{{count}} item(s) reset across {{sections}} section(s)."; on
  failure useMutationToast posts an error toast; SudoCanceledError is no-oped. Every conditional branch (per-row
  busy, the two confirm flows, the typed gate, success vs failure, the sudo-cancel swallow) and every t() key was
  read end-to-end and reproduced 1:1. Charts/maps: none. States in source: the section is ALWAYS rendered (the
  two catalogs are constant data — no data-gated hide, no mount-time fetch).

