PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  GlassPanel / IconBox    → tsGlassPanel() material + a tinted SF-Symbol box (ResetIconBox: cyan→accent,
                            amber→statusWarning, red→statusDanger); the Danger zone adds the web red border stroke.
  Button (variants)       → TSButton (.ghost per-row / .destructive Danger-zone + confirms / .secondary cancel)
                            via ResetActionButton, with the web `disabled` dim + a busy spinner applied at the wrapper.
  ConfirmDialog (danger)  → a destructive .sheet (red callout + Cancel + Reset); `loading` → the confirm spinner.
  ConfirmDialog (typed)   → a .sheet whose "Reset everything" stays disabled until the monospaced field == "RESET"
                            (ResetAdapter.isTypedConfirmationSatisfied: trims, case-sensitive); web parity 1:1.
  useToast().success      → an auto-dismissing capsule toast (title + "%lld item(s)…%lld section(s)." detail).
  useMutationToast().error→ the same toast tinted danger, with the per-scope message (web toast.settings.reset.error
                            / .allError); SudoCanceledError → SettingsResetCanceled, swallowed (no toast).
  per-row busy            → ResetModel.isSectionBusy(row) = sectionBusy && pending?.id == row.id (web 1:1).
  flex-wrap / divide-y    → ViewThatFits(.horizontal) row→column · Divider().overlay(Color.TS.border).
  i18n                    : zero English literals in code; every string via ResetStrings (table "ResetSection");
                            counts via String(format: "%1$lld…%2$lld…"); the RESET sentinel is a fixed literal (web parity).
  a11y                    : section is one VoiceOver container; each row .combine's title+description; every button
                            has an accessibilityLabel + .isButton; the typed field + toast are labeled; decorative
                            glyphs hidden; Dynamic Type (fixedSize wraps) + Reduce Motion (toast spring) respected.
  telemetry               : view.opened surface="ResetSection" once on start (P1/S11); previews use a no-op sink,
                            tests a spy that asserts the single emission.

STATES (every state renders; honest mapping for a mutation-only surface — no fabricated query states)
  loading  → a reset in flight: the affected control shows a TSButton spinner + is disabled (per-row for a section
             reset, the Danger-zone CTA + confirm for the global reset). The three panels stay fully rendered.
  empty    → N/A by construction: the section + deny-list catalogs are constant and non-empty (web useMemo lists);
             nothing is ever hidden — the "no hidden surfaces" rule is satisfied trivially.
  error    → a mutation failure surfaces the danger-tinted toast (web useMutationToast) while the content stays put.
  stale /  → N/A: there is no cached query to be stale about and no connectivity read in the web source; an offline
  offline    reset simply fails the mutation → the error toast. No fake skeleton / stale-chip / offline-chip was
             invented (that would be drift). Covered by previews (busy sheet, success + failure toast) + tests.

