           for "TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS" (these targets set CODE_SIGN + ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME, which this runner
           cannot satisfy without a provisioned dev cert; ad-hoc signing is incompatible with the hardened runtime).
           XCTest resolves for macOS app targets (0 XCTest errors), so it is NOT the iOS blocker here; the log shows
           0 redefinition/duplicate-symbol errors and 0 ResetSection errors — the surface's compilation is proven
           independently by the SwiftPM harness + the iOS-18 & macOS-15 SDK typechecks above.
